    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-09-30"></period-end>
     <target value="65.00"></target>
     <actual value="0.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">One activation for Pakistan floods.



On August 20, 2024, the model was activated for the first time after the national flood trigger was breached for 20 districts, with lead times ranging from 0 to 3 days across different regions. Of these 20 districts, the Start Network initiated proposals from its members in 11. Five of these members began implementing activities within 1-2 days of the model&apos;s activation, as their chosen districts (as indicated in their contingency plans at the beginning of the risk season) were projected to be highly impacted by the floods. However, reports from these members have yet to be submitted, making it difficult to determine whether anticipatory actions were taken. 



According to UNOSAT, the crisis peaked between August 20 and 26, while JBA&#x2019;s seasonal report suggested that the highest national impact occurred on August 19, with an estimated 2.9 million people affected across Pakistan. The remaining six members began their interventions around a month later, on September 13, 2024, focusing solely on early response activities due to delays in decision-making and processes aimed at reaching the most vulnerable districts.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-10-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="65.00"></target>
     <actual value="100.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Philippines: The DRF system in the Philippines was further activated for &#xA3;462,000 due to the increased impact of the cyclone on at-risk communities and given that additional municipalities were impacted within Cagayan. The system Philippines was designed to allow for multiple activations as a cyclone progresses. Start Ready was the ONLY mechanism activated for Cyclone Kristine. Members were able to successfully implement anticipatory action programming 42 hours before the cyclone made landfall. The DRF system for Zimbabwe drought also activated before the peak of the crisis.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
